# The Imperfectionist- Seventy Per Cent

![rw-book-cover](https://readwise-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/static/images/article0.00998d930354.png)

## Metadata
- Author: [[Oliver Burkeman]]
- Full Title: The Imperfectionist- Seventy Per Cent
- Category: #articles
- Summary:: The 70% rule suggests that if you're about 70% happy or confident with something, you should go ahead and share or act on it. This approach helps you overcome perfectionism and encourages taking action despite uncertainty. By doing so, you build resilience and prove to yourself that you can contribute without needing everything to be perfect.

## Highlights
- [[the 70% rule]]: If you’re roughly 70% happy with a piece of writing you’ve produced, you should publish it. If you’re 70% satisfied with a product you’ve created, launch it. If you’re 70% sure a decision is the right one, implement it. And if you’re 70% confident you’ve got what it takes to do something that might make a positive difference to the increasingly alarming era we seem to inhabit? Go ahead and do that thing. ([View Highlight](https://read.readwise.io/read/01jjzf8e3ntraxv7pw07fmna8z))
